{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A confirmed merge can be reported as needing review or landing when the saved PR snapshot is absent or stale."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"A digest can request another review while a changes round is running and cannot accept one."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An external push can invalidate an acknowledged approval without causing the digest to show that review is needed."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A previously blocked landing remains in the digest after the PR has been confirmed merged."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A large unacknowledged backlog can delay session startup through an unbounded sequence of per-run requests, although live latency was not measured."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"outage","trigger":"unusual","reason":"An exceptionally long stored question can fill or exceed an agent session's context when the digest inserts it in full."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An incomplete or older PR observation can cause status to report an outdated failed review round despite a later approval."},{"id":"C11","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"MCP review approvals are persisted and reported as coming from a human, giving incorrect audit provenance."},{"id":"C12","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Following the Codex skill can make its digest use Claude's acknowledged cursor and omit activity still unread by Codex."}]}